%% SLRU page-state machine for one slot.

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> EMPTY: SimpleLruInit
    EMPTY --> READ_IN_PROGRESS: SimpleLruReadPage<br/>start I/O
    READ_IN_PROGRESS --> VALID: I/O complete<br/>(buffer_locks released)
    READ_IN_PROGRESS --> EMPTY: I/O error
    EMPTY --> VALID: SimpleLruZeroPage<br/>(synchronous, no I/O)
    VALID --> VALID: re-read / re-mark dirty
    VALID --> WRITE_IN_PROGRESS: SimpleLruWritePage<br/>(dirty → flushing)
    WRITE_IN_PROGRESS --> VALID: I/O complete,<br/>!re_dirtied
    WRITE_IN_PROGRESS --> WRITE_IN_PROGRESS: re-dirtied while writing<br/>page_dirty stays true
    VALID --> EMPTY: SlruSelectLRUPage evicts<br/>(or SimpleLruTruncate)

    note right of VALID
        page_dirty bit decoupled from
        SlruPageStatus enum.
        bank_lock guards transitions;
        buffer_locks guards I/O.
    end note
